{"content_hash": "abf424affbcf3c33", "version_id": 434, "article_id": 44, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Fury-Joshua tickets sell out in an hour, priced up to £13,000", "title_zh": "富里对约书亚门票一小时售罄，最高票价达1.3万英镑", "has_translation": true, "topic": "sports", "source": "bbc_sport", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/boxing/articles/cwp9gxzyplk4o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788550545592-7e07d7846c76?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8ZnVyeSUyMHNwb3J0cyUyMGFjdGlvbnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTk0NTEyfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Daniel Delgado on Unsplash", "author": "Daniel Delgado", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@dannyd_91?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/people-grappling-in-jiu-jitsu-academy-x4A1siYHags?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(296, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(334, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SPORTS", "seed": "14d85ff3aedb"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 256, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Tickets for the heavyweight fight between Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua sold out in just one hour. The most expensive seats cost over £13,000, and resale prices are already much higher.", "lead_zh": "泰森·富里与安东尼·约书亚的重量级拳赛门票仅一小时就售罄。最贵的座位超过1.3万英镑，而二手票价已被炒得更高。", "preview": "Tickets for the all-British heavyweight fight between Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua at Cardiff's Principality Stadium sold out within one ho", "preview_zh": "泰森·富里与安东尼·约书亚的全英重量级拳赛门票在加的夫公国球场开售仅一小时便售罄。约8万张门票于周五中午开售，几分钟后就有超过50万人在线排队。最贵门票含手续费为13,128英镑，最便宜为88.50英镑。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 424, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/44/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 112.975, "size_bytes": 681696, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 297, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0a373f3/content/data/versions/434.json", "paragraphs": ["Tickets for the all-British heavyweight fight between Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua at Cardiff's Principality Stadium sold out within one hour. Around 80,000 tickets went on sale at noon on Friday, and more than 500,000 people were waiting online just minutes later. The highest-priced tickets cost £13,128 including fees, while the cheapest were £88.50.", "The fight will be shown globally on Netflix, and the event begins on 11 December, though the boxers are not expected to enter the ring until the early hours of 12 December. Ringwalks are planned for around 01:00 GMT, after a short live music performance, and the stadium will stay open until 03:30.", "Tickets quickly appeared on resale websites. Ringside VIP seats were advertised for £73,645, while upper-tier seats were offered for £425. The event is promoted by Saudi boxing powerbroker Turki Alalshikh's The Ring and UFC chief Dana White, but no undercard fights have been confirmed yet.", "Joshua, 36, and Fury, 38, are both former two-time world champions. They signed contracts earlier this year, but the date and venue were only confirmed later. Wembley Stadium in London and Madison Square Garden in New York were considered first, yet both had problems before Cardiff was chosen as an alternative.", "The Principality Stadium has hosted late-night boxing before, including Joe Calzaghe's fight in 2007. Just 11 days ago, the fight was in doubt because of a dispute over White's promotional role, but the British rivals met at a news conference on 30 September. They are reported to share a purse worth nearly $200m."], "paragraphs_zh": ["泰森·富里与安东尼·约书亚的全英重量级拳赛门票在加的夫公国球场开售仅一小时便售罄。约8万张门票于周五中午开售，几分钟后就有超过50万人在线排队。最贵门票含手续费为13,128英镑，最便宜为88.50英镑。", "这场比赛将在Netflix上全球直播，活动于12月11日开始，但预计两位拳手要到12月12日凌晨才会登台。入场仪式计划在格林尼治标准时间凌晨1点左右进行，之后有简短的音乐表演，球场将开放至凌晨3点30分。", "门票很快出现在二手网站上。场边VIP座位标价73,645英镑，上层看台座位标价425英镑。该赛事由沙特拳击经纪人图尔基·阿拉尔希赫的《拳台》杂志和UFC总裁达纳·怀特联合推广，但垫场赛尚未确认。", "36岁的约书亚和38岁的富里都曾两度获得世界冠军。他们今年早些时候签署了合同，但日期和场地后来才确定。伦敦温布利球场和纽约麦迪逊广场花园曾是最初考虑的地点，但两者都有问题，之后加的夫成为替代选择。", "公国球场此前曾举办过深夜拳赛，包括2007年乔·卡尔扎格的比赛。就在11天前，由于怀特的推广角色引发争议，比赛能否举行尚不确定，但这两位英国对手于9月30日在新闻发布会上会面。据报道，他们的总奖金接近2亿美元。"], "body": "Tickets for the all-British heavyweight fight between Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua at Cardiff's Principality Stadium sold out within one hour. Around 80,000 tickets went on sale at noon on Friday, and more than 500,000 people were waiting online just minutes later. The highest-priced tickets cost £13,128 including fees, while the cheapest were £88.50.\n\nThe fight will be shown globally on Netflix, and the event begins on 11 December, though the boxers are not expected to enter the ring until the early hours of 12 December. Ringwalks are planned for around 01:00 GMT, after a short live music performance, and the stadium will stay open until 03:30.\n\nTickets quickly appeared on resale websites. Ringside VIP seats were advertised for £73,645, while upper-tier seats were offered for £425. The event is promoted by Saudi boxing powerbroker Turki Alalshikh's The Ring and UFC chief Dana White, but no undercard fights have been confirmed yet.\n\nJoshua, 36, and Fury, 38, are both former two-time world champions. They signed contracts earlier this year, but the date and venue were only confirmed later. Wembley Stadium in London and Madison Square Garden in New York were considered first, yet both had problems before Cardiff was chosen as an alternative.\n\nThe Principality Stadium has hosted late-night boxing before, including Joe Calzaghe's fight in 2007. Just 11 days ago, the fight was in doubt because of a dispute over White's promotional role, but the British rivals met at a news conference on 30 September. They are reported to share a purse worth nearly $200m.", "body_zh": "泰森·富里与安东尼·约书亚的全英重量级拳赛门票在加的夫公国球场开售仅一小时便售罄。约8万张门票于周五中午开售，几分钟后就有超过50万人在线排队。最贵门票含手续费为13,128英镑，最便宜为88.50英镑。\n\n这场比赛将在Netflix上全球直播，活动于12月11日开始，但预计两位拳手要到12月12日凌晨才会登台。入场仪式计划在格林尼治标准时间凌晨1点左右进行，之后有简短的音乐表演，球场将开放至凌晨3点30分。\n\n门票很快出现在二手网站上。场边VIP座位标价73,645英镑，上层看台座位标价425英镑。该赛事由沙特拳击经纪人图尔基·阿拉尔希赫的《拳台》杂志和UFC总裁达纳·怀特联合推广，但垫场赛尚未确认。\n\n36岁的约书亚和38岁的富里都曾两度获得世界冠军。他们今年早些时候签署了合同，但日期和场地后来才确定。伦敦温布利球场和纽约麦迪逊广场花园曾是最初考虑的地点，但两者都有问题，之后加的夫成为替代选择。\n\n公国球场此前曾举办过深夜拳赛，包括2007年乔·卡尔扎格的比赛。就在11天前，由于怀特的推广角色引发争议，比赛能否举行尚不确定，但这两位英国对手于9月30日在新闻发布会上会面。据报道，他们的总奖金接近2亿美元。", "text": "Tickets for the all-British heavyweight fight between Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua at Cardiff's Principality Stadium sold out within one hour. Around 80,000 tickets went on sale at noon on Friday, and more than 500,000 people were waiting online just minutes later. The highest-priced tickets cost £13,128 including fees, while the cheapest were £88.50. The fight will be shown globally on Netflix, and the event begins on 11 December, though the boxers are not expected to enter the ring until the early hours of 12 December. Ringwalks are planned for around 01:00 GMT, after a short live music performance, and the stadium will stay open until 03:30. Tickets quickly appeared on resale websites. Ringside VIP seats were advertised for £73,645, while upper-tier seats were offered for £425. The event is promoted by Saudi boxing powerbroker Turki Alalshikh's The Ring and UFC chief Dana White, but no undercard fights have been confirmed yet. Joshua, 36, and Fury, 38, are both former two-time world champions. They signed contracts earlier this year, but the date and venue were only confirmed later. Wembley Stadium in London and Madison Square Garden in New York were considered first, yet both had problems before Cardiff was chosen as an alternative. The Principality Stadium has hosted late-night boxing before, including Joe Calzaghe's fight in 2007. Just 11 days ago, the fight was in doubt because of a dispute over White's promotional role, but the British rivals met at a news conference on 30 September. They are reported to share a purse worth nearly $200m.", "vocab": [{"word": "heavyweight", "pos": "noun", "zh": "重量级拳手", "note": "拳击术语，指体重最大的级别"}, {"word": "sell out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "售罄", "note": "常用短语，表示门票等全部卖完"}, {"word": "resale", "pos": "noun", "zh": "转售", "note": "指二手交易，常与 tickets 搭配"}, {"word": "ringside", "pos": "adj", "zh": "场边的", "note": "指靠近拳击台或擂台的位置"}, {"word": "purse", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奖金", "note": "体育比赛中指选手获得的总奖金"}, {"word": "promoter", "pos": "noun", "zh": "推广人", "note": "负责组织和宣传赛事的人"}, {"word": "undercard", "pos": "noun", "zh": "垫场赛", "note": "主赛之前的辅助比赛"}, {"word": "venue", "pos": "noun", "zh": "场地", "note": "举办活动的场所"}, {"word": "alternative", "pos": "noun", "zh": "替代方案", "note": "可数名词，常与 to 连用"}, {"word": "dispute", "pos": "noun", "zh": "争议", "note": "指意见不合或纠纷"}, {"word": "broadcast", "pos": "verb", "zh": "播出", "note": "常用被动语态，如 be broadcast globally"}, {"word": "collaboration", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合作", "note": "常与 between 连用，表示两者之间的合作"}], "title_original": "Fury-Joshua tickets priced up to £13,000 sell out in one hour", "summary_original": "Tickets for Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua's fight at Cardiff's Principality Stadium sells out in just one hour.", "body_original": "Fury-Joshua tickets priced up to £13,000 sell out in one hour\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nTickets for Tyson Fury and Anthony Joshua's fight at Cardiff's Principality Stadium have sold out in just one hour.\nFury and Joshua will meet on a bill that begins on 11 December but they are not expected to fight until the early hours of 12 December.\nThe highest-priced tickets were available at £13,128, including booking fees, with the lowest at £88.50.\nThe all-British heavyweight contest, which will be broadcast globally on Netflix, was\nannounced in September\nand around 80,000 tickets went on sale at 12:00 BST on Friday.\nJust minutes after the tickets went on sale more than 500,000 people were waiting in the online queue.\nTickets quickly began emerging on resale websites, with ringside VIP seats being advertised for £73,645, while upper tier seats were available for £425.\nRingwalks are\nexpected to start around 01:00 GMT\non Saturday 12 December, following a short live music performance, and the stadium will remain open until 03:30.\nThe event is being promoted as a collaboration between Saudi boxing powerbroker Turki Alalshikh's The Ring and UFC chief Dana White.\nOrganisers are yet to confirm any of the undercard fights.\nWhat information do we collect from this quiz?\nJoshua, 36, and Fury, 38 - both former two-time world champions - signed contracts for the bout earlier this year, but the date and venue had yet to be confirmed.\nLondon's Wembley Stadium and New York's Madison Square Garden were the frontrunners to stage the fight, but both presented issues before Cardiff emerged as an alternative.\nThe Principality Stadium has hosted late-night boxing before, including Joe Calzaghe's fight with Mikkel Kessler in November 2007, which began at 01:00 GMT.\nRicky Hatton's victory over Kostya Tszyu at Manchester's MEN Arena in 2005 began at about 02:00 local time, allowing US broadcaster Showtime to show the fight on Saturday evening.\nJust 11 days ago, there was uncertainty over whether the fight would even take place due to a dispute over the role of UFC chief White in the promotion of the event.\nBroadcaster Netflix said Alalshikh's The Ring and White would collaborate to promote the event, but Joshua's promoter Eddie Hearn said his fighter's contract prevented White from having a promotional role.\nThe British rivals finally met at a news conference on 30 September to begin the build-up to one of the most anticipated fights in British history.\nFury and Joshua are reported to be sharing a purse worth close to $200m (£151m)\nRelated topics\nBoxing\nBoxing schedule and results 2026\nPublished\n1 day ago\nWatch every Born to Brawl episode\nPublished\n28 April 2024\nMore boxing from the BBC\nNotifications, social media and more with BBC Sport\nPublished\n28 August", "fe